0264, 13, 151646, 151016, 154879, 25, 154511, 149910, 150011, 185020, 67, 156793, 150407, 153103, 182507, 149880, 152979, 171656, 13, 200010, 200001, 200004, 4115, 220, 16, 25], "text": "Step 1: Total sum of all K_i is S. Assigning each department to Group A or Group B, the two group totals sum to S. We need to minimize the larger of the two totals. This is equivalent to finding the smallest possible absolute difference between Group A and Group B, because the larger total is (S + |difference|)/2.\n\nStep 2: Since N <= 20, enumerate all 2^N assignments. For each assignment, compute the Group A total. The Group B total is S - A. The maximum of the two is max(A, S - A). Keep the minimum over all assignments.\n\nStep 3: Return the minimum over all assignments.\n\nFinal:\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = list(map(int, data[1:1 + n]))\n    total = sum(k)\n    best = None\n    for mask in range(1 << n):\n        a = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            if mask & (1 << i):\n                a += k[i]\n        b = total - a\n        m = max(a, b)\n        if best is None or m < best:\n            best = m\n    print(best)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```<|end_message|><|content_model_end_sampling|>", "points": {"step2": 79, "step3": 139}, "tokens": [151613, 150811, 149879, 149971, 149958, 62, 72, 149884, 149936, 13, 175050, 279, 150154, 157866, 149882, 151775, 149897, 149918, 151775, 149939, 11, 149876, 150103, 150417, 150269, 82, 150811, 149882, 149936, 13, 150197, 150261, 149882, 173709, 149876, 153753, 149879, 149876, 150103, 150269, 82, 13, 150078, 149884, 153654, 149882, 156169, 149876, 169444, 150564, 154405, 151572, 150134, 151775, 149897, 149880, 151775, 149939, 11, 150301, 149876, 153753, 150269, 149884, 196976, 50, 196986, 196975, 71964, 91, 8, 14, 17, 13, 68014, 4115, 220, 17, 25, 152943, 149977, 197012, 220, 68020, 11, 158195, 149971, 220, 17, 61, 45, 187177, 13, 150194,